  "visual_review": [
    "Base zone11/13 images inspected on Compatibility and zone11 on desktop Mobile; LiA10/26 inspected on Compatibility. Foam follows the authored canyon drop, with small lip/impact spray and mist near the visible pool.",
    "Graphics: 21 images at800x600 across EN/RU/DE. New Water, World and Weather controls fit with existing controller/touch navigation and Original look/Back rows."
  ],
  "evidence": [
    "Analytic6m coherent step admits one drop; .75m/cell rapid, isolated spike, burial, map border, excessive width and nonfinite levels reject. Flooding/removal/restoration is deterministic.",
    "Synthetic type4 half-metre XY jitter recovers the complete authored tile; mixed owner/sign-bit decoding retained, lava owner and swamp tile omitted.",
    "62 complete zone*.mpr map loads; seven matched sites admit lip, impact and mist roles. Ground and navigation arrays stay unchanged during detection.",
    "All three desktop renderers pass held-clock pixels, flow visibility, flood coalescing, disable/dependency restoration and retirement. Negative zone8 adds0 draws and changes0 pixels. Positive sites add2 draws.",
    "Graphics UI336 assertions cover all effect reachability, mouse/controller/touch navigation, translated labels/help, default/preset exclusion and existing wave/cover setting persistence."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Desktop RTX3090 only. No Android, Windows, handheld or browser execution claim and no FPS/device-cost claim.",
    "Census timings are non-isolated diagnostic construction costs, not frame benchmarks. Detection/rebuild is script-based, synchronous and only on enable/level changes; large or frequently flooded maps may hitch with this opt-in effect.",
    "Conservative classification can miss unusual hand-authored falls. It is a visual overlay over existing water, not hydraulic simulation or terrain geometry replacement.",
    "Rendered fixtures load real terrain with controlled camera/light; full gameplay scenery/crowds and every newly detected campaign alias were not separately rendered.",
    "Compatibility emits the existing screen-space-AA availability warning at boot; accepted runs have no shader/script/runtime errors.",
    "Frozen QA base includes the wave checkpoint plus owned changes. Parallel ambient, cloud and dialogue changes are excluded from this isolated pack and need their own integration validation."
  ],
